{"id":"code-min-window","title":"Minimum window substring","category":"code","difficulty":4,"prompt":"Write a Python function `min_window(s: str, t: str) -> str` that returns the shortest substring of `s` containing every character of `t`, counting repeats (if `t` has two b's, the window needs two b's). If several windows share the shortest length, return the leftmost. If there is no such window, or `t` is empty, return an empty string. It should run in O(len(s) + len(t)) time.","system":"You are completing one task from an evaluation suite. Do the task as asked.\n\nReply with one Python code block that defines exactly what the task asks for. Use only the standard library. Do not include tests, examples, or print statements.","grader":{"type":"code","entrypoint":"min_window","tests":["assert min_window(\"ADOBECODEBANC\", \"ABC\") == \"BANC\"","assert min_window(\"a\", \"a\") == \"a\"","assert min_window(\"a\", \"aa\") == \"\"","assert min_window(\"aa\", \"aa\") == \"aa\"","assert min_window(\"abc\", \"\") == \"\"","assert min_window(\"bba\", \"ab\") == \"ba\"","assert min_window(\"abcabc\", \"ca\") == \"ca\"","assert min_window(\"xaybzaxb\", \"ab\") == \"ayb\"","assert min_window(\"aabdccb\", \"abb\") == \"abdccb\"","assert min_window(\"abc\", \"d\") == \"\""]},"reference":"```python\nfrom collections import Counter\n\ndef min_window(s: str, t: str) -> str:\n    if not t or len(t) > len(s):\n        return \"\"\n    need = Counter(t)\n    missing = len(t)\n    best = (0, 0)\n    left = 0\n    for right, ch in enumerate(s, 1):\n        if need[ch] > 0:\n            missing -= 1\n        need[ch] -= 1\n        if missing == 0:\n            while need[s[left]] < 0:\n                need[s[left]] += 1\n                left += 1\n            if best == (0, 0) or right - left < best[1] - best[0]:\n                best = (left, right)\n            need[s[left]] += 1\n            missing += 1\n            left += 1\n    return s[best[0]:best[1]]\n```","answers":["```python\ndef min_window(s: str, t: str) -> str:\n    if not t:\n        return \"\"\n    need = set(t)\n    best = \"\"\n    for left in range(len(s)):\n        seen = set()\n        for right in range(left, len(s)):\n            if s[right] in need:\n                seen.add(s[right])\n            if seen == need:\n                if not best or right - left + 1 < len(best):\n                    best = s[left:right + 1]\n                break\n    return best\n```","```python\nfrom collections import Counter\n\ndef min_window(s: str, t: str) -> str:\n    if not t or len(t) > len(s):\n        return \"\"\n    need = Counter(t)\n    missing = len(t)\n    best = (0, 0)\n    left = 0\n    for right, ch in enumerate(s, 1):\n        if need[ch] > 0:\n            missing -= 1\n        need[ch] -= 1\n        if missing == 0:\n            while need[s[left]] < 0:\n                need[s[left]] += 1\n                left += 1\n            if best == (0, 0) or right - left < best[1] - best[0]:\n                best = (left, right)\n            need[s[left]] += 1\n            missing += 1\n            left += 1\n    return s[best[0]:best[1]]\n```"],"cells":[{"arm":"haiku-low","trial":0,"mode":"sync","status":"ok","score":0.7,"passed":false,"answer":0,"details":{"passed":7,"total":10,"tests":[{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":false,"error":"AssertionError"},{"ok":false,"error":"AssertionError"},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":false,"error":"AssertionError"},{"ok":true}],"simulated":{"pass_probability":0.024,"answer":"known-wrong"}},"input_tokens":189,"output_tokens":324,"cost_usd":0.0001809,"latency_ms":1944.4},{"arm":"haiku-low","trial":1,"mode":"batch","status":"ok","score":0.7,"passed":false,"answer":0,"details":{"passed":7,"total":10,"tests":[{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":false,"error":"AssertionError"},{"ok":false,"error":"AssertionError"},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":false,"error":"AssertionError"},{"ok":true}],"simulated":{"pass_probabi